WEBVTT

00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:12.397
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> The girl looked out the window dreamily.

00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:14.561
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘Mr Hartley,’

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:16.339
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> she said slowly,

00:00:16.785 --> 00:00:18.999
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘I don’t know what to say to you.

00:00:19.514 --> 00:00:22.552
I understand all the advantages of your offer,

00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:26.655
and sometimes I feel sure that I could be happy with you.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:30.763
But, then sometimes I am less sure.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.124
I was born a city girl,

00:00:33.287 --> 00:00:37.554
and I am not sure that I would enjoy living a quiet life in the suburbs.’

00:00:38.176 --> 00:00:39.575
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘My dear girl,’

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.995
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said Hartley,

00:00:41.584 --> 00:00:43.730
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘You will have everything that you want.

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:46.665
You can come to the city for the theatre,

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:51.126
for shopping, and to visit your friends as often as you want.

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:54.013
You can trust me, can’t you?’

00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:56.450
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘I can trust you completely,’

00:00:56.877 --> 00:00:58.970
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> she said, smiling at him.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:02.253
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘I know you are the kindest of men,

00:01:02.657 --> 00:01:05.681
and that the girl who you get will be very lucky.

00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:09.327
I heard all about you when I was at the Montgomerys’.’

00:01:09.538 --> 00:01:10.293
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘Ah!’

00:01:10.568 --> 00:01:11.826
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> exclaimed Hartley,

00:01:12.292 --> 00:01:16.863
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘I remember so well the evening I first saw you at the Montgomerys’.

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:19.504
I will never forget that dinner.

00:01:20.693 --> 00:01:23.216
Come on, Vivienne, promise me.

00:01:24.158 --> 00:01:25.158
I want you.

00:01:25.542 --> 00:01:29.095
Nobody else will ever give you such a happy home.’

00:01:29.878 --> 00:01:31.380
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> Vivienne didn’t answer.

00:01:32.136 --> 00:01:34.737
Suddenly Hartley was suspicious.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.743
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘Tell me, Vivienne, is there…’

00:01:38.106 --> 00:01:38.905
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> he asked,

00:01:39.246 --> 00:01:40.744
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘…is there someone else?’

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.366
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘You shouldn't ask that, Mr. Hartley,’

00:01:43.522 --> 00:01:44.289
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> she said.

00:01:44.645 --> 00:01:46.045
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘But I will tell you.

00:01:46.562 --> 00:01:50.936
There is one other person…but I haven’t promised him anything.’

00:01:50.961 --> 00:01:51.683
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘Vivienne,’

00:01:51.816 --> 00:01:53.414
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> said Hartley masterfully.

00:01:53.724 --> 00:01:55.704
<v><b>Hartley:</b></v> ‘You must be mine.’

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.570
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> Vivienne looked him in the eye.

00:01:59.478 --> 00:02:01.771
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘Do you think for one moment,’

00:02:01.897 --> 00:02:03.311
<v><b>Reader:</b></v> she said calmly,

00:02:03.604 --> 00:02:07.997
<v><b>Vivienne:</b></v> ‘that I could come to your home while Héloise is there?’